MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: d913a4144935222419bce97051219529, type: 3}
  m_Name: IntroCutsceneDefinition
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: ProjectGame2D.Runtime::IntroCutsceneDefinition
  _cutsceneId: cutscene.intro.orynthals
  _segments:
  - _segmentId: intro.logo
    _displayName: Logo Intro
    _video: {fileID: 32900000, guid: c6afc4acf13141c468bb350bbec1099e, type: 3}
    _lines: []
  - _segmentId: intro.story.firelight
    _displayName: The First Spark
    _video: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 88a53e790f59c8248acd6388f25649f4, type: 3}
    _lines:
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: In the days of chaos, when all things still churned and clung to one
        another, only to break apart again, the world was much like a shore beneath
        a raging storm. Waves came and went, and what was born one moment might
        be gone the next.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: Then came the Proto-Deities.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: So the old tales tell it, they were a mischievous lot — greedy, curious,
        and never quite content. They built the first sandcastles of the world.
        They shaped the seas, wove the forests, raised the mountains, and made the
        beasts that dwelt upon the land.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: Then they poured life into them.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: But that was not enough. The deities breathed one more thing into the
        world — the wind of freedom.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: And so the living things began to grow on their own, to change, and
        to find their own ways. Before long, those little sandcastles were brimming
        with life.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: Perhaps... that was how the world came to be.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: But the waves of Chaos still rolled on. And one day, no one knows quite
        when, some of those waves ceased to draw back into the sea.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: They crawled upon the shore, swept through the forests, and reached
        lands that were once peaceful. Wherever they went, living things changed.
        Beasts became things no one had ever seen, and trees began to grow things
        that ought not to grow.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: The folk called it the Incursion.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: And why did it come? No one knows. Even the Gods, it seems, knew not
        why they vanished. Well... tales of the gods are tales of the gods. Who
        can say?
  - _segmentId: intro.story.departure
    _displayName: A Promise at Dawn
    _video: {fileID: 32900000, guid: c371b62259b89c74bafb6b79f96e31d9, type: 3}
    _lines:
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: Strange thing is, the world did not die. Where the waves had swallowed
        the land, new life would grow again. Ash turned green once more. One thing
        faded away, and another took its place.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: The world would grow, and then it would wither. Then it would grow
        again. No one knows what it shall become the next time.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: And then, no one quite knows when, there were people too. They built
        their homes, sowed their fields, hunted, traded. And whenever the waves
        came, they simply built again.
  - _segmentId: intro.story.open-road
    _displayName: The Road Calls
    _video: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 84b46b8dc9d154941a68a36aeb369e23, type: 3}
    _lines:
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: But not all folk wished to stay. Some took up their packs and walked
        towards lands where others dared not tread. They came to be called Wayfarers.
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: They were not all heroes. Most were simply folk who had chosen to walk
        that road, each for their own reason.
  - _segmentId: intro.story.village
    _displayName: The Village of Beginnings
    _video: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 3fb0dbfa87b134544a729b25b8c46c35, type: 3}
    _lines:
    - _speakerName: Bard
      _text: And then, one day... another Wayfarer set foot upon that road.
  - _segmentId: intro.story.training-yard
    _displayName: A Guide Appears
    _video: {fileID: 32900000, guid: 2f2c972fbff0a2249a50baa96d061b6e, type: 3}
    _lines:
    - _speakerName: Cenhelm
      _text: Well now... a face I don't recognize. You must have come from somewhere
        beyond our little village. Welcome, traveler. I'm Cenhelm, the village elder.
        Welcome to Heorte.
    - _speakerName: Frawand
      _text: Frawand. I'm a Wayfarer. Been on the road for a while.
    - _speakerName: Cenhelm
      _text: A Wayfarer, eh? Then you've come a long way. You'd best rest your feet
        for a while. Stay with us if you like. There's room enough in the village,
        and I can show you around.
  - _segmentId: intro.outro.transition
    _displayName: Into the Village
    _video: {fileID: 32900000, guid: f9422df3995cd804bad417dce54a79ae, type: 3}
    _lines: []
